{title: Sunshine}
{artist: Jonathan Edwards}
{key: A}
{duration: 3:00}
{tempo: 125}


{start_of_part: Intro}
[A]
{end_of_part}


{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Sunshine go away today
I don't feel much like [E]dancing
[A]Some man's gone, he's tried to run my life
Don't know what he's [D]asking
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]He tells me I'd better get in line
Can't hear what he's [E]saying
When [A]I grow up I'm going to make it mine
But these aren't dues I been [D]paying
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]How much does it cost,[A] I'll buy it
The [D]time is all we've lost,[A] I'll try it
But [D]he can't even run[A] his own life
I'll be [G]damned if he'll run mine,[E] Sunshine
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Sunshine go away today
I don't feel much like [E]dancing
[A]Some man's gone, he's tried to run my life
Don't know what he's [D]asking
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Working starts to make me wonder where
The fruits of what I do are [E]going
[A]He says in love and war all is fair
But he's got cards he ain't [D]showing
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]How much does it cost,[A] I'll buy it
The [D]time is all we've lost,[A] I'll try it
But [D]he can't even run[A] his own life
I'll be [G]damned if he'll run mine,[E] Sunshine
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[A]Sunshine come on back another day
I promise you I'll be [E]singing
[A]This old world, she's gonna turn around
Brand new bells'll be [D]ringing
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_part: Outro}
[D] [A/D] [Bmadd11/D] [D] [A/D] [Bmadd11/D][A]
